The Game Manager
The game manager is basic in this game, and you can add it first. To create the game manager,
follow these steps:
1. Create an empty game object and name it GameManager.
2. Because the only asset you have for the game manager is a script, create a new folder
called Scripts so that you have a place for any simple scripts you create.
3. Create a new script named GameManager in the Scripts folder and attach it to the
GameManager game object. Overwrite the contents of the script with the following code:
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI; // Note this new line is needed for UI
public class GameManager : MonoBehaviour
{
public Text scoreText;
public Text gameOverText;
int playerScore = 0;
public void AddScore()
{
playerScore++;
// This converts the score (a number) into a string
scoreText.text = playerScore.ToString();
}
public void PlayerDied()
{
gameOverText.enabled = true;
// This freezes the game
Time.timeScale = 0;
}
}
